    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d809">

                <pb facs="0821" n="709" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg709"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.24/174: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Commission to
                        Negotiate Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-09T20:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 9,
                                1919, 8 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>3074. For Polk; also Hoover. President has approved charter of 45,000 tons of
                    shipping to Russian Embassy here for transporting supplies from British and
                    French ports to forces of General Yudenitch. Embassy now negotiating with
                    Shipping Board.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
